import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base search={false} crumbs={[['Legal','/legal/'],['AI disclosure','/legal/ai-disclosure/']]} title="AI disclosure" description="How ADITEJUS uses AI to produce its lessons, and what is always real.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="ph"><h1>AI disclosure</h1><p class="faint">Last updated: 31 October 2026 (draft for creator approval)</p></header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="todo">TODO (creator): confirm every line below before launch.</p>
      <h2>Where we use AI</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Narration.</strong> Many videos are narrated with an AI voice model trained on the creator's own voice.</li>
        <li><strong>Production help.</strong> AI tools help draft scripts, code examples and visuals. A person decides what is published.</li>
        <li><strong>This website.</strong> Parts of the site were built with AI assistance. Course and lesson facts come from our published syllabus, not from AI guesses.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What is always real</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Demos are real runs: real tools on real tasks, recorded for that lesson. No mock-ups presented as real.</li>
        <li>Numbers on this site are counted from our syllabus at build time. We do not publish invented learner numbers or testimonials.</li>
        <li>Claims about how companies use AI are sourced and dated.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>On other platforms</h2>
      <p>On YouTube we use the altered or synthetic content setting where it applies. Every Udemy course description begins with the line Udemy requires: “This course contains the use of artificial intelligence.”</p>
      <h2>Animations on this site</h2>
      <p>The agent animation on the home page is a scripted replay of steps taught in a lesson, and is labelled as such.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
